# Number rules for Chinese (zh, Mainland China). Chinese writes no spaces, so the numerals are single characters that the recognizer
# combines by position (三百二十五, 一千零五, 三万五千) instead of words it looks up in a table.
#
# Format: [section] headers, then one rule per line, fields separated by "|". "#" starts a comment.

[number.digits]
system | chinese
decimal | .
group | ,
negative | -−

# Digits, in the plain and the financial (capital) forms, 零 and 〇 for zero, 两 for two before a unit.
[zh.digit]
零, 〇 | 0
一, 壹 | 1
二, 贰, 貳, 两, 兩 | 2
三, 叁, 參 | 3
四, 肆 | 4
五, 伍 | 5
六, 陆, 陸 | 6
七, 柒 | 7
八, 捌 | 8
九, 玖 | 9

# Ten, hundred, thousand.
[zh.small]
十, 拾 | 10
百, 佰 | 100
千, 仟 | 1000

# Ten thousand and a hundred million: a group of four digits is counted in them (三亿五千万).
[zh.big]
万, 萬 | 10000
亿, 億 | 100000000

[zh.word]
point | 点
negative | 负
ordinal | 第
percent | 百分之
hundred | 百
fraction | 分之
# A single numeral character (三, 十, 两) is a number only before one of these counting words: 三个人, 两只猫. Not 统一, 一些, 之一.
classifier | 个, 只, 条, 位, 名, 件, 本, 张, 次, 天, 种, 家, 台, 辆, 把, 双, 对, 套, 份, 场, 间, 座, 首, 部, 头, 瓶, 杯, 口, 人, 页, 篇, 封, 支, 根, 颗, 粒, 棵, 朵, 片, 道, 项, 段, 局, 层, 届, 批, 组, 圈, 例, 辈
# A small unit of money is not money before these characters: 三角形, 三毛钱 stays.
notmoney | 形, 色, 度, 板
rangeto | 到, 至, -, ~, ～, —, –, －
from | 从, 自
every | 每个, 每
everyother | 每隔
daily | 天天
later | 后, 以后, 之后, 过后
ago | 前, 以前, 之前
gap | 零, 又, 加
andahalf | 个半
firsthalf | 上半年
secondhalf | 下半年
quarter | 季度
weekend | 周末
monthearly | 初, 上旬
monthmid | 中旬
monthlate | 下旬, 底, 末

[percent]
%, ％

# Telephone numbers: mobile numbers are eleven digits starting 13 to 19 (written together or as 3-4-4), landlines an area code
# (0 and two or three more digits) and seven or eight digits joined by a hyphen.
[phone.plain]
13, 14, 15, 16, 17, 18, 19 | 11

[phone.area]
0 | 3-4 | 7-8

[phone.space-start]
1 | 11 | 11
